# Rank Tracker Pro — configuration

Copy this file to `.env` and edit. Every value is optional: with no `.env` at all
the app boots in demo mode (mock SERP provider, SQLite in `data/`, scheduler on).

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

## Core

| Variable | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `NODE_ENV` | `development` | `production` enables secure cookies and quiet logs |
| `PORT` | `4170` | HTTP port |
| `HOST` | `0.0.0.0` | bind address |
| `DATA_DIR` | `./data` | SQLite database + generated secret live here |
| `DB_FILE` | `$DATA_DIR/rank-tracker.db` | override to put the DB elsewhere |
| `SESSION_SECRET` | generated | keeps sessions valid across restarts; set it in production |
| `SESSION_DAYS` | `14` | cookie lifetime |
| `COOKIE_NAME` | `rt_session` | |
| `COOKIE_SECURE` | `false` | set `true` behind HTTPS |
| `ALLOW_BOOTSTRAP` | `true` | first-run account creation; only works while `users` is empty |

## Search data

| Variable | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SERP_PROVIDER` | `auto` | `auto` picks serper → serpapi → mock |
| `SERPER_API_KEY` | – | [serper.dev](https://serper.dev) — cheapest per query, 2500 free |
| `SERPAPI_API_KEY` | – | [serpapi.com](https://serpapi.com) — 100 free/month |
| `SERP_TIMEOUT_MS` | `20000` | per request |

With no key the **mock** provider is used: deterministic fake rankings so the UI,
charts and alerts all work offline. It never touches the network.

## Alerts

| Variable | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `TELEGRAM_ENABLED` | `false` | |
| `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` | – | from @BotFather |
| `TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID` | – | your numeric chat id |
| `GOOGLE_SHEETS_ENABLED` | `false` | |
| `GOOGLE_SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL` | – | Apps Script Web App URL (see `docs/deploy.md`) |
| `GOOGLE_SHEETS_ID` | – | spreadsheet id, for the link in the UI |
| `GOOGLE_SHEETS_TOKEN` | – | shared secret sent as `?token=` |
| `EMAIL_ALERTS_ENABLED` | `false` | |
| `EMAIL_WEBHOOK_URL` | – | any endpoint that accepts `{to,subject,html}` |
| `EMAIL_ALERT_TO` | – | default recipient |
| `EMAIL_WEBHOOK_TOKEN` | – | shared secret sent as `?token=` |

A delivery channel that is not configured simply reports `skipped` in the run
summary — nothing fails.

## Integrations (optional, read-only)

| Variable | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GSC_ENABLED` | `false` | Search Console: real impressions/clicks next to rank |
| `GSC_PROPERTY` | – | `sc-domain:example.com` or the URL-prefix property |
| `GSC_CLIENT_EMAIL` | – | service-account email |
| `GSC_PRIVATE_KEY` | – | service-account key, `\n` escaped is fine |
| `GA4_ENABLED` | `false` | |
| `GA4_PROPERTY_ID` | – | numeric property id |
| `GA4_CLIENT_EMAIL` / `GA4_PRIVATE_KEY` | – | service account |
| `CRUX_ENABLED` | `false` | Chrome UX Report field data |
| `CRUX_API_KEY` | – | |

## Scheduler & limits

| Variable | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SCHEDULER_ENABLED` | `true` | background job runner (60 s tick) |
| `SCHEDULER_INTERVAL_MINUTES` | `60` | how often the runner wakes |
| `SCHEDULER_RUN_ON_BOOT` | `false` | catch up on missed jobs at start |
| `MAX_KEYWORDS` | `500` | per user |
| `MAX_SITES` | `20` | per user |
| `MAX_SESSIONS_PER_DAY` | `5000` | budget guard, per user |

## Full example

```env
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=4170
HOST=0.0.0.0
DATA_DIR=./data
SESSION_SECRET=change-me-32-bytes-minimum
COOKIE_SECURE=true

SERP_PROVIDER=serper
SERPER_API_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

TELEGRAM_ENABLED=true
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456:ABC-DEF...
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=123456789

GOOGLE_SHEETS_ENABLED=true
GOOGLE_SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL=https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfy.../exec
GOOGLE_SHEETS_TOKEN=shared-secret

EMAIL_ALERTS_ENABLED=true
EMAIL_ALERT_TO=me@example.com
EMAIL_WEBHOOK_URL=https://your-worker.example.com/email
EMAIL_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=shared-secret

SCHEDULER_ENABLED=true
SCHEDULER_INTERVAL_MINUTES=60
```
